 the name of the wizarding school that Harry attends?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and Wizardry has four houses: Gryffindor, Hufflepuff, Ravenclaw, and Slytherin.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-acdf-7110-a4f9-724241350918","description":"Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and Wizardry","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-acdf-7aad-838f-1417c7f16f10","description":"Ilvermorny School of Witchcraft and Wizardry","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-acdf-7143-bd00-22b0f733877d","description":"Durmstrang Institute of Magic","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-acdf-72f7-a25a-7d64a2ce83bf","description":"Beauxbatons Academy of Magic","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-acdf-72ed-9dfc-a86abc494980","category":"01a21312-b489-7dba-9459-62cdf152de47","question":"Which Italian artist shocked 1485 Florence with his large nude painting of the birth of a goddess?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Botticelli\'s The Birth of Venus shows the goddess arriving on shore in a giant scallop shell; the painting is now in Florence\'s Uffizi Gallery.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-acdf-77e7-9256-565b92cd0892","description":"Botticelli","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-acdf-7fd2-b0f7-d6dd719d6187","description":"Michelangelo","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-acdf-7e13-8efb-1da780fc8d9e","description":"Leonardo da Vinci","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-acdf-7216-9a86-356404b2a9c8","description":"Raphael","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-acdf-7ab1-9f16-970e486d4e17","category":"01a21312-b489-7dba-9459-62cdf152de47","question":"Which author wrote \'War and Peace\'?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Leo Tolstoy also wrote Anna Karenina. War and Peace follows Russian families during the Napoleonic invasion of Russia.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-acdf-7f53-a3b8-9c5866329e69","description":"Leo Tolstoy","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-acdf-74a8-88b8-bb71f611001f","description":"Ivan Turgenev","correct_answer":false},{"